"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkmy_website=globalThis.webpackChunkmy_website||[]).push([[7608],{1644(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"release-2-10","metadata":{"permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-10","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-07-Release-2.10.md","title":"Release 2.10","description":"\u2728 Main improvements:","date":"2026-03-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":1,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Stephane Couturier","title":"Developer of Katalog","url":"https://github.com/StephaneCouturier","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8320281?v=4","key":"StephaneCouturier","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"release-2-10","title":"Release 2.10","authors":["StephaneCouturier"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Release 2.9","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-9"}},"content":"\u2728 Main improvements:\\n\\n- **#723 BACKUP: Incremental BackUp from source Catalog to target Catalog**\\n- **#738 BACKUP: Archive (move) files from source Catalog to target Catalog**\\nIt is now possible to Backup (incremental copy) or Archive (move) files using the catalog links defined in the [BackUp]( https://stephanecouturier.github.io/Katalog/docs/BackUp) screen.\\n\\n- **#713 CREATE: Exclude folders / folder paths per catalog or globally**\\nOn Create or Devices edit screen, it is now possible to add folders to be excluded with the Catalog itself. The feature to exclude globally from collection remain on screen Create.\\n\\n- **#728 Linux packaging: Flathub/Flatpak version**\\nEnabled a Flatpak version hosted on Flathub (application on Flathub in progress)\\n\\n\u26a0\ufe0f Technical changes:\\n- As for any new version, it is highly recommended to **backup the collections** \ud83d\udcbe, and test the new version on other copies.\\n- **Database updates**: added fields to support backup improvements\\n\\n\ud83d\udce6 Distribution Formats:\\n- As usual, **Window 64**, **Linux**, **macOS**\\n- **Flathub/Flatpak** has been prepared and will be added soon to Flathub for easier Linux deployment\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Release details:\\n- Full list of updates: https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/issues?q=milestone%3A2.10+sort%3Acreated-asc\\n- Full code changelog: https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/compare/v2.9...v2.10\\n- \ud83d\udce5 **Download Katalog**: https://sourceforge.net/projects/katalogg\\n- \ud83d\udcda **Documentation**: https://stephanecouturier.github.io/Katalog"},{"id":"release-2-9","metadata":{"permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-9","source":"@site/blog/2026-02-07-Release-2.9.md","title":"Release 2.9","description":"\u2728 Main improvements:","date":"2026-02-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":1.69,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Stephane Couturier","title":"Developer of Katalog","url":"https://github.com/StephaneCouturier","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8320281?v=4","key":"StephaneCouturier","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"release-2-9","title":"Release 2.9","authors":["StephaneCouturier"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Release 2.10","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-10"},"nextItem":{"title":"Release 2.8","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-8"}},"content":"\u2728 Main improvements:\\n\\n- **#664 CREATE/SEARCH: File Checksum SH256 for Duplicate/Difference Search**\\nIt is now possible to compute and store files checksum in the catalogs.\\nIt is a **much longer process** than other indexing option as **it reads ALL of the data** to compute the checksums.\\nLike file metadata, the option can be selected at catalog creation or changed later, and when interrupting the process, the calculated checksum are saved and the next update will resume for remaining files.\\nThe files checkum can be used as a duplicate search option or as a difference search option\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n- **#402 DATA: Store data in a local MySQL/mariadb database.**\\nBeside Memory or SQLite File modes, it is now possible to store data in a local hosted db.\\nFor the local machine, it can present a good compromise between speed of indexing vs speed of searching.\\nIt is **ONLY for USE with LOCAL** hosted db (ex: MySQL server installed on the computer using Katalog).\\nCommunication to a remote database would not be encrypted nor secured.\\n\\n- **#675 BACKUP: Generate LuckyBackup profile from BackUp links**\\nMostly for Linux users, the catalog links (mappings) done in the tab BackUp can now be used to generate a LuckyBackup profile.\\nThese are basic profiles (task name, source, destination), no exclude or advanced options.\\n\\n- **#692 SEARCH Duplicates: new option to compare 2 devices**\\n\\n\u26a0\ufe0f Technical changes:\\n- As for any new version, it is highly recommended to **backup the collections** \ud83d\udcbe, and test the new version on other copies.\\n- **Database updates**: added fields to store checksum and new search duplicates options\\n\\n\ud83d\udce6 Distribution Formats:\\n- As usual, **Window 64**, **Linux**, **macOS**\\n- Reminder: **AppImage** is available for easier Linux deployment, including one for older/LTS distributions with glibc 2.35 (ex: Ubuntu 22..04) It is still possible to use the Command Line Interface with AppImage.\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Release details:\\n- Full list of updates: https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/issues?q=milestone%3A2.9+sort%3Acreated-asc\\n- Full code changelog: https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/compare/v2.8...v2.9\\n- \ud83d\udce5 **Download Katalog**: https://sourceforge.net/projects/katalogg\\n- \ud83d\udcda **Documentation**: https://stephanecouturier.github.io/Katalog"},{"id":"release-2-8","metadata":{"permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-8","source":"@site/blog/2025-11-09-Release-2.8.md","title":"Release 2.8","description":"\u2728 Main improvements:","date":"2025-11-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":1.89,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Stephane Couturier","title":"Developer of Katalog","url":"https://github.com/StephaneCouturier","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8320281?v=4","key":"StephaneCouturier","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"release-2-8","title":"Release 2.8","authors":["StephaneCouturier"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Release 2.9","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-9"},"nextItem":{"title":"A test of QML and Kirigami for Katalog","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/2024/09/05/Testing-QML-and-Kirigam"}},"content":"\u2728 Main improvements:\\n\\n- #379 CREATE/ SEARCH: **File Types** management\\n   Instead of hard-coded and limited list, Katalog now uses a **standard database, with more than 1200 known types**, to determine the type from the extension and it can also verify the real mime type and report gaps.\\nThe definition of main types \\"Images, Audio, Video\\" is strictly related, only the type \\"Text\\" was customized to include types such as PDF. see [Create#file-type-categories](https://stephanecouturier.github.io/Katalog/docs/Create#file-type-categories)\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n- #379 CREATE/ SEARCH: **File Metadata** management\\nBasic Media (Image size, Video duration, Music artist, etc.) or Extended (all available) metadata can be scanned, stored, and used in searching. see [Create#metadata-extraction](https://stephanecouturier.github.io/Katalog/docs/Create#metadata-extraction) for the different options.\\n**Important**: indexing metadata is a much, **much slower process** than just indexing them. (ex: 45minutes for 100 000 files)\\nWhich is why it comes with another new major feature: \\n- #662 DEVICES: **Incremental update**\\nUpdating a device will only process new or modified files, which is a critical need to save time when using File Metadata and avoid re-scanning them when files have not changed.\\n   \\n- #660 CREATE/ SEARCH/DEVICES: consistent operations **progress reporting** in  status bar\\n\\n\u26a0\ufe0f Technical changes:\\n- As for any new version, it is highly recommended to **backup the collections** \ud83d\udcbe, and test the new version on other copies.\\n- **Database update**: significant changes have been made as fields were added to store metadata\\n- **Catalogs migration**: all catalog will require an operation to populate the new file_types & mime-types. This will happen only once, per catalog, and when using Search or Explore for the first time.\\n\\n\ud83d\udce6 Distribution Formats:\\n- New!  Katalog is now provided for **Apple macOS** (dmg file or zip)  note: **\u26a0\ufe0f Katalog was not tested on macOS**, feedback is very welcome\\n- Reminder: AppImage is available for easier Linux deployment, including one for older/LTS distributions with glibc 2.35 (ex: Ubuntu 22..04) It is now the default version when downloading from on SourceForge. It is still possible to use the Command Line Interface with AppImage\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Release details:\\n- Full list of updates: https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/issues?q=milestone%3A2.8+sort%3Acreated-asc\\n- Full code changelog: https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/compare/v2.7...v2.8\\n- \ud83d\udce5 **Download Katalog**: https://sourceforge.net/projects/katalogg\\n- \ud83d\udcda **Documentation**: https://stephanecouturier.github.io/Katalog"},{"id":"/2024/09/05/Testing-QML-and-Kirigam","metadata":{"permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/2024/09/05/Testing-QML-and-Kirigam","source":"@site/blog/2024-09-05-Testing-QML-and-Kirigam.md","title":"A test of QML and Kirigami for Katalog","description":"Looking at the future of Katalog, a few direction have been here since the start of the project:","date":"2024-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"pre-development","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/tags/pre-development"}],"readingTime":0.76,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Stephane Couturier","title":"Developer of Katalog","url":"https://github.com/StephaneCouturier","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8320281?v=4","key":"StephaneCouturier","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"title":"A test of QML and Kirigami for Katalog","authors":["StephaneCouturier"],"tags":["pre-development"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Release 2.8","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-8"},"nextItem":{"title":"Major Release 2.0","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-0"}},"content":"Looking at the future of Katalog, a few direction have been here since the start of the project:\\n- Multi-platform: why not even consider Mobile ? (ok, iOS should really be covered first)\\n- Using KDE KF6 librairies: this could be the best way to grow capabilities such a archives indexing or media files meta data\\n- User Experience: nicer interface, more responsive.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nIt happens that there is now a way to address all that at once: QML with Kirigami\\n- QML is the modern interface design code from Qt (which makes 100% of Katalog today)\\n- Kirigami is the QML based framework by KDE to provide additional interface and consistency in the KDE world.\\n\\nWell, so far it works :)\\nInstallation of the Kirigami:\\n- Linux (using kdebuild)\\n- Windows (using Craft)\\n\\nInterface\\n- globaldrawer\\n- pages for each former tab\\n\\nBackend / C++\\n- Basic Search function, connection to a collection database file and returning results based on the text criteria:"},{"id":"release-2-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/release-2-0","source":"@site/i18n/fr/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2024-05-04-Major-Release-2-0.md","title":"Major Release 2.0","description":"Apr\xe8s avoir publi\xe9 1 version de Katalog chaque mois et comme aucun bug majeur n\'avait \xe9t\xe9 signal\xe9, les versions ont \xe9t\xe9 suspendues depuis juillet dernier pour permettre de travailler sur cette prochaine grande version.","date":"2024-05-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":1.1,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Stephane Couturier","title":"Developer of Katalog","url":"https://github.com/StephaneCouturier","imageURL":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8320281?v=4","key":"StephaneCouturier","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"release-2-0","title":"Major Release 2.0","authors":["StephaneCouturier"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"A test of QML and Kirigami for Katalog","permalink":"/Katalog/fr/blog/2024/09/05/Testing-QML-and-Kirigam"}},"content":"Apr\xe8s avoir publi\xe9 1 version de Katalog chaque mois et comme aucun bug majeur n\'avait \xe9t\xe9 signal\xe9, les versions ont \xe9t\xe9 suspendues depuis juillet dernier pour permettre de travailler sur cette prochaine grande version.\\n\\nVoici enfin la release 2.0 : [Release Notes](https://github.com/StephaneCouturier/Katalog/releases/tag/v2.0)\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nCe d\xe9veloppement s\'est concentr\xe9 sur 2 principaux catalyseurs\xa0:\\n- **P\xe9riph\xe9riques**\xa0: les listes de p\xe9riph\xe9riques virtuels, de stockage et de catalogue sont d\xe9sormais toutes accessibles \xe0 partir d\'un seul onglet fournissant l\'\xe9quivalent sur les 3 onglets pr\xe9c\xe9dents. Il offre la flexibilit\xe9 de cr\xe9er une **hi\xe9rarchie globale d\'appareils** pour am\xe9liorer les fonctionnalit\xe9s de recherche ou de statistiques.\\n\\n- Les **donn\xe9es** peuvent d\xe9sormais \xeatre g\xe9r\xe9es dans un **fichier de base de donn\xe9es** (format SQLite), tout en conservant la possibilit\xe9 de conserver les fichiers CSV traditionnels. Cela permettra \xe9galement une future option pour h\xe9berger la base de donn\xe9es sur un serveur.\\n\\nCes changements impliquaient des mises \xe0 jour majeures du mod\xe8le de donn\xe9es et de la gestion des donn\xe9es.<br/>\\nPar cons\xe9quent, la version prend en charge une proc\xe9dure de migration 1.x > 2.0.\\n\\n&#9888; **Sauvegardez auparavant les donn\xe9es de votre collection Katalog cr\xe9\xe9es avec les versions pr\xe9c\xe9dentes**. &#9888;\\n\\nPour en savoir plus sur ces principaux changements, explorez les pages *P\xe9riph\xe9riques* et *Param\xe8tres* de la Documentation.\\n\\nTous les commentaires via Facebook, Github, e-mail sont toujours appr\xe9ci\xe9s \ud83d\ude09"}]}}')}}]);